  "assumptions": [
    "All task, capacity, response, power and heat values are synthetic screening inputs. They are not measured HAPS, drone, gateway or cloud platform specifications.",
    "The measurement window is 60 seconds and the per-task response values are synthetic end-to-end values with the metric basis declared for each task.",
    "All three workloads must complete 100% within their declared response budgets; no task is silently dropped or converted to best effort.",
    "The HAPS power budget and HAPS heat-rejection budget are additional incremental limits for this example, not vehicle-wide propulsion/thermal ratings.",
    "For HAPS placement, node_power_w and node_waste_heat_w are the compute-side HAPS loads; haps_network_power_w and haps_network_waste_heat_w are additional HAPS communication loads to reach remote compute nodes.",
    "For non-HAPS placement, node_power_w and node_waste_heat_w are charged to the destination node; HAPS network power, heat and backhaul are charged separately to the HAPS.",
    "HAPS incremental power is HAPS-node compute power plus HAPS network power. HAPS waste heat is HAPS-node waste heat plus HAPS network waste heat.",
    "Total system power is the sum of all selected node power and HAPS network power; it is not the same as HAPS incremental power.",
    "The all-platform baseline is intentionally infeasible: combined compute demand 2.55 TOPS, power 110 W and heat 99 W exceed the HAPS node/whole-platform budgets.",
    "The lowest-latency feasible comparator assigns alert fusion and wildfire analytics to HAPS and drone control to the drone, yielding 155 priority-weighted response-ms and 113 W total system power.",
    "The minimum-system-power assignment places alert fusion and drone control on HAPS and wildfire analytics at the terrestrial gateway, yielding 93 W total system power while satisfying all deadlines and limits.",
    "The exhaustive oracle enumerates all 3 × 4 × 3 = 36 allowed combinations and minimizes total system power over feasible assignments; no learned model is used in this tiny fixture.",
    "The fixture is a scheduler arithmetic benchmark only. It contains no measured network paths, queueing distributions, thermal-fluid simulation, HVAC/cooling model, battery chemistry, HAPS propulsion, flight dynamics or safety validation.",
    "The Sceye / SoftBank reported 68 ms value is an average round-trip processing response in one source-attributed trial; it is not used as an input or as a direct p95/p99 comparison target."
